   570	  // number. checkDispatchPolicy now refuses a malformed record upstream (so a string
   571	  // maxRuntimeMinutes never reaches here), but we re-assert it directly rather than
   572	  // trusting the type: a non-number ceiling would otherwise be silently discarded by
   573	  // the timeout computation and codex would run with the caller timeout instead of
   574	  // the intended bound. Fail closed rather than spawn without an enforced ceiling.
   575	  // Bug10 (defense-in-depth): the runtime ceiling MUST be a real, finite, positive
